<title>BAHRAIN: Islamic bank lends Egypt iron, steel firm $20 mln.</title>
<headline>Islamic bank lends Egypt iron, steel firm $20 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Islamic Development Bank (IDB) said on Monday it would lend Alexandria National Iron and Steel $20 million to finance production needs.</p>
<p>An IDB statement said two agreements for the loan were signed in Jeddah on Monday.</p>
<p>The Jeddah-based IDB was set up in 1975 to help finance and promote trade exchanges between Islamic states.</p>
</text>
